{
  "dom_id": "step-q38583",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255664/assets/b96ff81f993dbb42d58d81427b6e3d9712d93f20431ae7ec64544e94d6c63595.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The degree of $P(x)$ is even.\n\nII. The coefficient of the leading term is positive.\n\nIII. $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$",
  "worked_solution": "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is positive.\n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true.",
